{"text": "To:\nFron:\n\nSubject:\n\nPHILIP MORRIS U. S. A.\nINTER-OFFICE CORRESPONDENCE\nRICHMOND, VIRGINIA\n\nE. F. Pierce\n\nJanuary 22, 1986\nR. He Cox\n\nDetermination of Menthol in Filter Plugs\n\nAttached, please find a method for the determination of the presence of\nmenthol in filter plugs that was developed by Bill Harvey. This method\ncould be used to insure that trays of plugs are labeled correctly before\nthey are placed on the maker. If you or your people have questions\nregarding this method, I would suggest that you contact Bill Harvey at\nExtension 5955. We will continue to try to develop a method for the\n\ndetermination of menthol in plugs on-line but I don't forsee a usable method\nin the near future,\n\nAlso, 2s I indicated to you during C. Horner's meeting on January 21,\nwe have examined menthcl retains from the flavor Center for levels of minor\nmenthol isomers. The synthetic menthol is very clean and consistent with\nonly isomenthol being detected at low levels. The natural menthol samples\nshow the presence of several minor menthol isomers as expected. However,\nthe levels of these isomers appear to be relatively consistent from batch to\nbatch, The results for both the synthetic and natural menthols are\nattached. Please advise if further information is required.\n\nAttachment\n\nRHC/ jm KiCy\n\nC86-20961\n\nLEBLLOOOS",
